course: dictionary
lesson: 12020
title: Chitin, the tough outer shell
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: Some words name a material, the stuff that something is made from. Chitin is one of these. Read the context: «The beetle's chitin shell was hard and shiny.» The shell is hard, so chitin must be a tough material that makes a shell strong.
explain: Science books use chitin for the hard outside of many creatures. «Insects, spiders and crabs have a skeleton of chitin on the outside of their bodies.» Their skeleton is outside, not inside like ours, so chitin does the job that bones do for us.
explain: Chitin also makes the walls of fungi, such as mushrooms. «The fungus has cell walls made of chitin.» Here chitin is not a shell, but a tough wall around each tiny cell.
fact: Chitin is a tough natural material.
fact: Chitin makes up the hard outer skeleton of insects, spiders, crabs and lobsters.
fact: Chitin is also found in the cell walls of fungi.
fact: «Exoskeleton» means a skeleton on the outside of the body.
fact: Creatures with a chitin shell must moult, which means shed the old shell, in order to grow.
exercise: «Insects have a hard outer skeleton made of chitin.» What is chitin? | A soft, wet kind of moss | A kind of bone found inside the body | A type of wing | *A tough natural material
exercise: «A lobster must shed its chitin shell to grow.» What does moult mean? | Paint the shell a bright red | Eat a very big meal | *Shed, or take off, the old shell | Break the shell in two
exercise: Maya says, «Spiders and crabs have bones inside, like us, so chitin must be the stuff of bones.» Is Maya right? | Yes, chitin is found in bones inside the body | Yes, chitin is a kind of soft flesh | No, chitin is a kind of plant | *No, their hard skeleton is on the outside and is made of chitin
test: «Fungi have cell walls made of chitin.» Where is chitin found in fungi? | *In the cell walls | In the roots of trees | In the blood | In the wings
test: Which creature has a hard outer skeleton made of chitin? | *A crab | A frog with soft skin | A worm with no shell | A cat
exam: «The beetle's chitin shell stayed hard, even in the sun.» What is the chitin? | *A tough natural material for the outer skeleton | A kind of wood | A bright coloured paint | A soft jelly under the skin
